      <h2 id="not-protein">Where collagen sits against your protein intake</h2>

      <p>
        Collagen is a protein, but it is a bad one for building muscle. It contains no tryptophan
        at all, which makes it an incomplete protein by definition, and it is low in leucine, the
        amino acid that triggers muscle protein synthesis. Counting your 10g collagen shot towards
        your daily protein target is a mistake many men make.
      </p>

      <p>
        Whey does the muscle job. Collagen does the connective tissue job. They are not competitors
        and they are not substitutes, which is a point worth its own article, so the full
        comparison lives in <a href="/pages/collagen-vs-whey-protein">collagen vs whey protein</a>.
        The table below is only the summary a man standing in a shop needs.
      </p>

