      <h2 id="dose">Dose, timing and a realistic schedule</h2>

      <p>
        Take 10g of hydrolysed collagen daily with vitamin C, and if tendons are your reason for
        taking it, take it 30 to 60 minutes before you train rather than after. Judge joint results
        at 12 weeks, not at two.
      </p>

      <p>
        Here is where I have to be inconvenient about our own product. Skelecoll provides
        <strong>10,000mg of hydrolysed marine collagen per 30ml shot</strong>, which matches the
        10g used in Clark's 24 week athlete trial and sits above the 5g used by Zdzieblik. It is
        below the 15g that Shaw's group used in the pre-training gelatin protocol. If you are
        specifically chasing the tendon adaptation effect at the studied dose, one shot does not
        get you to 15g, and I would rather you knew that before you bought it than after.
      </p>

      <p>
        The vitamin C side is covered: Skelecoll includes <strong>40mg of vitamin C from amla</strong>,
        which is above the Indian RDA and sufficient for the cross-linking enzymes. Shaw's protocol
        used a higher vitamin C load, though the enzymes involved saturate at modest concentrations,
        so I would not lose sleep over that gap.
      </p>

